  "summary": "The Millbrae City Council approved a five-year, $293,000 contract with Flock Safety to install 23 automated license plate reader cameras around major transit arteries, citing concerns about organized crime. The article describes the technology, hot-list functionality, 30-day retention by Flock (with possible longer retention under San Mateo County Sheriff's policy), and notes recent state-level concerns including Sen. Wiener's legislation and ALPR data sharing with ICE by Pasadena and Long Beach police.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Millbrae will soon get a host of new surveillance cameras, with the City Council approving a five-year contract to install 23 license plate reading devices around major transit arteries in the city.",
      "paragraph_idx": 0
    },
    {
      "quote": "The five-year cost to Millbrae, including initial setup fees, will be $293,000.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    },
    {
      "quote": "Per the San Mateo County Sheriff's Office policies on ALPR use, however, data collected could be transferred elsewhere before deletions from Flock storage and stored for up to one year.",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    },
    {
      "quote": "Police in Pasadena and Long Beach were found to have shared ALPR captured data with U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement last year, despite the state's sanctuary law",
      "paragraph_idx": 18
    }
  ],
